      "side": 1,
      "message": "As Matthias mentioned in the chat, this will suppress CRC mismatches, however the ABI tools are looking at the `!__GENKSYMS__` and still including them in the KMI so changes to `struct fscrypt_keyring` will still trigger ABI failures in TH.\n\nTo allow post-freeze changes, you might want to add some padding:\n- `ANDROID_BACKPORT_RESERVED()` for future backports\n- `ANDRIOID_VENDOR_DATA()` a/o `ANDROID_OEM_DATA()` for partner use\n- `ANDRIOD_KABI_RESERVE()` for LTS update use",
